  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "When Fang An Lei is struck he holds her, tries healing methods that fail, and screams that Suan Bu Jin lured the attack. He names himself Fang Chen before Fang Yuan cuts him off. Fang Hua Sheng chides him and tells Fang Yuan he is Fang An Lei’s husband, worried for his wife. Fang Yuan reads that he married into Fang clan as a recruited lone immortal, changed his surname after the marriage, and after the scolding lowers his head to keep checking Fang An Lei even though his methods are useless.",
      "chapters": [
        1519
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_an_lei",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_fang_hua_sheng",
        "fac_fang_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "His expression changes during compensation talks, and he is stunned when Fang Yuan demands payment even for a bad mood. After Fang An Lei’s injuries are stabilized, he sends her back to Fang clan headquarters unconscious.",
      "chapters": [
        1520
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ally-talks-and-escort",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He is among Fang clan’s six Gu Immortals facing Divine Bean Palace’s side under Fang Hua Sheng.",
      "chapters": [
        1522
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ally-talks-and-escort",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "house_divine_bean_palace"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In discussion hall with the supreme elders he grits his teeth that Suan Bu Jin was Fang Yuan, blames the clan’s ostracism on that demon, and refuses association. He argues that dealing with Fang Yuan would give righteous path forces a bigger excuse to isolate the clan, then falls silent when Fang Di Chang lets Fang Leng finish proposing secret compliance. He judges himself an outsider married into the clan whose status wastes his talents, fit only as a superficial stepping stone for Fang Leng.",
      "chapters": [
        1616
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "soul-cores-debate",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_di_chang",
        "char_fang_leng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is very excited when told An Lei can really be revived.",
      "chapters": [
        2263
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "return-with-an-lei",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Leng later says Fang An Lei and Fang Chen have returned, and Fang Chen sighs that the plan is as expected of Lord Fang Di Chang.",
      "chapters": [
        2273
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "return-with-an-lei",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
